  "evidence": "TEXT_F: Emphasises national identity and sovereignty (“in Europe, not run by Europe”; keep the pound; reject euro; renegotiate Nice; embed reserved powers); restrictive asylum policy (secure reception centres, presumption of refusal from safe countries, dedicated removals); strong law-and-order (more police, tougher drug laws, honest sentencing, lifetime supervision for sex offenders); bolster traditional institutions (Married Couple’s Allowance; expand faith/parent/charity schools); robust defence posture (maintain independent deterrent, support missile defence, exempt forces from ECHR). TEXT_G: Social-liberal and environmental commitments (votes at 16; inclusive citizenship; PR; end asylum voucher system on humanitarian grounds; ambitious renewables, no new nuclear); pro‑EU stance (subsidiarity, full EU representation with independence); demilitarising tendencies (remove Trident; oppose US missile defence; phased NATO withdrawal); some law‑and‑order elements (1,000 more police; tougher on dealers; lifelong supervision for high‑risk sex offenders); national identity via Scottish independence.",
  "reasoning": "TEXT_F consistently argues from TAN priorities—order, tradition, national sovereignty, and restrictive asylum—aligning with a slightly TAN-leaning electorate. TEXT_G mixes nationalism with predominantly GAL commitments (social liberalisation, environmentalism, pro‑EU, humanitarian asylum), placing it relatively closer to GAL than the profile.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "winner": "TEXT_F"
}
